WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.170
To celebrate the release of Pitch Perfect
2, let's take a look at 12 things you probably

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.150
didn't know about the musical comedy sequel.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.389
To get ready for the movie's opening sequence,
which features her performing Miley Cyrus's

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:18.779
Wrecking Ball, Rebel Wilson trained in acrobatics
at LA's Cirque School with aerial stunts expert

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:20.250
Aloysia Gavre.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:25.420
Although in real life Wilson's afraid of heights,
she trained three times a week for five weeks

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.120
so she could swing using trapeze silks, and
perform moves including what she calls the

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.010
‘Death Drop Spread Eagle', in a routine
somewhat inspired by Pink's performance of

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.910
Glitter In the Air at the 2010 Grammy Awards.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.149
Costumes for Pitch Perfect 2, including the
Bellas' bodysuits for the opening sequence,

00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:46.930
feature 20,000 dollars' worth of Swarovski
crystals.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:52.850
The costume department employed three women
full time to crystallise costumes!

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:57.230
Thanks to the massive world-wide success of
Pitch Perfect and its soundtrack, licensing

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.550
songs for the sequel was a little easier.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:04.739
The toughest song to secure was Muse's Uprising,
which German group Das Sound Machine perform

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.909
in the movie, and which took a personal request
written by director Elizabeth Banks to Muse

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:12.670
frontman Matt Bellamy to lock down.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:19.220
After tweeting Alexis Knapp, American football
player David Bakhtiari managed to score a

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.020
cameo in Pitch Perfect 2 for himself and four
of his teammates from the Green Bay Packers.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.740
Bakhtiari and his fellow players, Clay Matthews,
Don Barclay, T.J.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:32.450
Lang and Josh Sitton, plus Jordan Rodgers,
who plays in the Canadian Football League,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:37.081
are such huge fans of the first Pitch Perfect
movie that, according to Anna Kendrick, they

00:01:37.081 --> 00:01:39.250
can do the finale back to front!

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:44.770
About a month before filming, the stars of
Pitch Perfect 2 gathered for an a capella

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.130
boot camp with the movie's music and choreography
team.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:53.770
Musical director and vocal producer Deke Sharon
made sure everyone could sing every note perfectly

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.920
from memory before they were allowed into
the recording studio to lay down their part

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.189
of each track.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:03.700
Whereas training for the first movie focused
on nailing the basics, in Pitch Perfect 2

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.399
the Barden Bellas have been a capella stars
for several years, so Sharon worked on extending

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:13.920
the actors' vocal techniques and ranges and
made them mimic instruments!

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.870
The movie's World Championships feature cameos
from a number of real-life a capella groups.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:23.560
Among those appearing are Pentatonix, who
hail from Texas and won US reality show The

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.430
Sing-Off, in 2011, and appear in the film
as Canadian group Mountain Rhythm.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:33.380
Also making an appearance are The Filharmonic,
an all-male Filipino-American a capella group

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.730
based in LA, who are called Manila Envy in
the movie.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.760
Also getting a cameo are Penn Masala, a Hindi
a capella group formed at the University of

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.830
Pennsylvania in the mid-90s, and who are called
The Naan Stops in Pitch Perfect 2.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:52.900
Sons Of Anarchy star Katey Sagal, who plays
the mother of new Barden Bella Emily, actually

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.730
has an off-screen connection to the world
of a capella, as her older daughter Sarah

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:01.620
White is in two a capella choirs, The Owl
Creek Singers and the Stairwells, at Kenyon

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.390
College in Ohio.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.230
Snoop Dogg wanted to be in Pitch Perfect 2
as his daughter is such a huge fan of the

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.230
first movie.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:13.120
So, the rapper makes a cameo appearance as
himself.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.350
Adam DeVine's Bumper and Rebel Wilson's Fat
Amy may be something of an item in the movie,

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:23.100
but in real life DeVine is dating Kelley Jakle,
who plays Wilson's fellow Barden Bella, Jessica.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.900
The pair met when they filmed the first Pitch
Perfect.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:32.170
As a student, Jakle was part of the SoCal
VoCals, a University of South California a

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:36.940
capella group that's won the International
Championship of Collegiate A Cappella, or

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.750
ICCAs, multiple times.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:43.240
Oh, and also in real life, Jakle and Brittany
Snow, who plays Chloe, are best friends and

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.200
share a home in LA!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.920
Skylar Astin plays Anna Kendrick's on-screen
boyfriend Jesse, but in real life his girlfriend

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.990
is Anna Camp, who plays former Bella Aubrey.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.483
And, like Adam DeVine and Kelley Jakle, Astin
and Camp also met on the original Pitch Perfect.

00:03:55.483 --> 00:04:00.260
The movie's a capella World Championships
may take place in Denmark's capital city Copenhagen,

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.300
but they were actually filmed in Highland
Park in Baton Rouge, Louisiana.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:09.570
A casting call was put out in the summer of
2014 and fans of the first film were invited

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:14.910
to attend the night-time shoot, which attracted
around 3,000 people.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:19.920
Other Baton Rouge locations in Pitch Perfect
2 included the Old Louisiana Governor's Mansion,

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.420
which was used for the Dean's house; a mansion
on Highland Road, which was used for the underground

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:29.560
a capella riff-off; and for exterior shots
of Barden University, the filmmakers and cast

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.230
returned to the Louisiana State University
where the original movie also filmed.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:38.430
Well there you have it, 12 things you probably
didn't know about Pitch Perfect 2!

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.620
Now, let me know in the comments below, what
are your favourite moments from the Pitch

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.410
Perfect movies and why?

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:46.710
And what songs would you love to hear if they
make a Pitch Perfect 3?

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.730
